differing: skills/work-planner/artifacts/board-queue.md ### Ready Unit Lanes
  --- skills/work-planner/artifacts/board-queue.md
  +++ skills/work-planner/artifacts/board-queue.md
  @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
   A Ready unit consists of free, undelivered task rows joined through [Joins](#joins), or one unjoined row. Every member meets [Task Eligibility](#task-eligibility) under its epic's proposed Ready or In Progress status. A reservation or an open delivery pull request holds its rows, as [Task Delivery](#task-delivery) states.
   
  -Each unit's lane comes from the raw task-table [Lane](#lane) cells in the supplied epic issue bodies, through the shared lane-cell reader. Joined rows carry one common index or all have empty cells. Report the index as `lane 2`, or empty cells as `unlaned`, including rows with no linked work item. Priority and delivery state determine the Status and assignee calls; lanes annotate the unit report.
  +Each unit meets [Unit Consistency](#unit-consistency) and carries its [Report Label](#report-label), including rows with no linked work item. Priority and delivery state determine the Status and assignee calls; lanes annotate the unit report.
