differing: skills/work-planner/artifacts/dependency-graph.md ### Joins
  --- skills/work-planner/artifacts/dependency-graph.md
  +++ skills/work-planner/artifacts/dependency-graph.md
  @@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
   The undelivered rows of one epic whose work items declare one [component](#component) are a candidate unit: one pull request writes that file once, where separate ones each rebase on the last. Rows declaring different components need no accounting.
   
   - **A joined unit has one lane.**
  -  Each row's [Lane](#lane) cell carries the same index, or every cell is empty. A split assignment is resolved by changing a row's lane or unjoining the rows.
  +  Joined rows meet [Unit Consistency](#unit-consistency).
   - **A candidate is answered once.**
     Its rows name each other in Joins, or one line of a record names exactly its rows and why they stay split. A line naming only some of its rows, or rows besides, accounts for none.
   - **Both resolutions are stated where the candidate is reported.**
